   "harm": "relying on external IPC clients rather than internal FIFO eviction to free template memory could lead to node OOM",
   "hash": "21281572c8b93bab",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T04:00:36+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:3493499544",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:3493499544",
   "kind": "approach",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "Delegating template eviction responsibility to the client can put us in a situation where they handle it poorly and cause us to OOM",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2025-11-24",
    "by": "Sjors",
    "id": "c:3570105870",
    "quote": "In the scenario where they handle it poorly, we can use FIFO deletion. All `getMemoryLoad()` does is give clients an opportunity to handle it better. If they're fine with FIFO, then they never have to call this method."
   },
   "status_note": "",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33922#pullrequestreview-3493499544"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-12-04",
   "author": "ryanofsky",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:2592303231"
   ],
   "clears_with": "change",
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "1647b291ccae0c0c5c79f0117adcbb0d73231221"
   },
   "harm": "template_tx_refs map accessed across multiple threads without synchronization creates data race hazards",
   "hash": "6fbffba75bb144d5",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T04:00:36+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2590041765",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2590041765",
   "kind": "safety",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "This map can updated from multiple threads, so it needs a mutex to be used safely.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "fixed",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2025-12-05",
    "by": "Sjors",
    "id": "rc:2592303231",
    "quote": "To limit the scope of this PR, I only added the mutex, but called it `template_state_mutex` in anticipation."
   },
   "status_note": "",
   "type": "objection",
